-- title:
--   Reduced source factors through the scheme-theoretic image
-- statement:
--   Let $X$, $Y$, $T$ be schemes, let $f \colon X \to Y$ be a quasi-compact morphism, and let $u \colon T \to Y$ be a morphism whose source $T$ is reduced. Assume the set-theoretic hypothesis that the range of the underlying continuous map of $u$ is contained in the topological closure of the range of the underlying continuous map of $f$, i.e. $u(T) \subseteq \overline{f(X)}$ inside the space of $Y$. Then $u$ factors through the scheme-theoretic image of $f$: there exists a morphism of schemes $v \colon T \to$ `f.image` such that $v$ followed by the canonical closed immersion `f.imageι : f.image ⟶ Y` equals $u$. Here `f.image` is the closed subscheme of $Y$ cut out by the ideal sheaf generated by the kernels of the maps $f^\sharp$ on sections, and `f.imageι` its inclusion. Only existence of the factorisation is asserted; its uniqueness (which holds, `f.imageι` being a monomorphism) is not part of the conclusion.
--
--   This is the standard universal property of the scheme-theoretic image for quasi-compact morphisms: a morphism from a reduced scheme meeting the closure of $f(X)$ set-theoretically factors scheme-theoretically through the image. It is used in the variant for integral sources ([`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.exists_lift_schemeTheoreticImage_of_isDomain`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.exists_lift_schemeTheoreticImage_of_isDomain)) and, further on, in constructions of relative group laws on Jacobians and in the production of closed immersions with prescribed rank in the Weierstrass-curve material.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_Hom_exists_lift_schemeTheoreticImage_of_isReduced.lean

